FRAMIC AI — SUPABASE INTEGRATION STANDARD

Repository:
davidsun2026-v1/framic-ai

Purpose:
Keep Framic AI's Supabase integration aligned with the existing Next.js architecture. Do not replace existing authentication or middleware files with generic Supabase tutorial code.

1. Environment variables

Use the existing Framic AI environment-variable convention.

File:
apps/web/.env.local

Required:

NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://gkvvecskbkwpcsuatklm.supabase.co
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=<SET_LOCALLY_ONLY>

IMPORTANT:
- Never commit .env.local.
- Never commit Supabase keys or secrets to GitHub.
- Do not paste the real key into source files, documentation, issues, PRs, screenshots, or chat.
- Keep production/service-role credentials server-side only.
- Do not replace NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY with a second publishable-key convention unless the repository architecture is intentionally migrated and verified.

2. Existing Framic AI authentication architecture

Use the existing implementation as the source of truth.

Relevant files:

apps/web/lib/auth/actions.ts
apps/web/lib/auth/middleware-utils.ts
apps/web/middleware.ts
apps/web/app/auth/callback/route.ts

Do not create duplicate authentication helpers unless an audit proves they are required.

3. Supabase SSR

Framic AI should use the Supabase SSR pattern appropriate for the installed versions of:

@supabase/supabase-js
@supabase/ssr

Server-side Supabase clients must preserve authenticated cookies/session handling.

Browser-side clients must use only public environment variables.

Service-role credentials must never be exposed to browser code.

4. Middleware

The existing Framic AI middleware is authoritative.

Any Supabase session-refresh implementation must be reconciled with:

apps/web/middleware.ts
apps/web/lib/auth/middleware-utils.ts

Do not overwrite middleware with the generic Supabase quickstart example.

5. Authentication

Authentication behavior must remain consistent across:

Sign up
Sign in
Sign out
Auth callback
Session refresh
Protected routes

Use the existing Framic AI implementation and database schema rather than the example "todos" table from Supabase documentation.

6. Database

Supabase is the authoritative backend source of truth for Framic AI.

Do not invent tables such as:

todos

Do not modify production Supabase data or schema unless explicitly authorized.

Schema changes must be represented through Supabase migrations and verified against the actual project state.

7. Security

Never place:

SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY

or any other privileged secret in:

Client components
Browser bundles
NEXT_PUBLIC_* variables
GitHub source files
README files
Documentation
Screenshots
Issues
Pull requests

If a credential has accidentally been exposed, rotate/revoke it through Supabase and replace the local environment value.

8. Agent Skills

Supabase Agent Skills are optional developer tooling.

If required for the development environment:

npx skills add supabase/agent-skills

Installing the skills does not replace or modify Framic AI's authentication architecture.

9. Verification requirement

Before declaring Supabase integration complete, verify:

[ ] Environment variables use the repository convention
[ ] No real credentials are committed
[ ] Supabase SSR dependencies are installed
[ ] Server client works
[ ] Browser client works where required
[ ] Middleware refreshes sessions correctly
[ ] Auth callback works
[ ] Protected routes enforce authentication
[ ] Sign up works
[ ] Sign in works
[ ] Sign out works
[ ] Typecheck passes
[ ] Production build passes

Status vocabulary:

VERIFIED
PARTIAL
BROKEN
NOT VERIFIED

Do not mark an item VERIFIED without repository or runtime evidence.
